---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
// Update this date whenever the policy changes. It is shown on the page.
const UPDATED = 'October 11, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How Long Press chooses what to publish, how each section works, how sources are linked, how money stays separate from the writing, and how corrections work."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Standards</span>
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        How Long Press decides what to publish, how each section works, and what happens when it is wrong.
      </p>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="publishes">What Long Press publishes</h2>
      <p>
        Three things: <a href="/daily">The Daily Five</a>, <a href="/known-issue">Known Issue</a> and <a href="/fine-print">Fine Print</a>. How each one is built is described on the <a href="/about">About page</a>. This page covers the rules that apply to all three.
      </p>

      <h2 id="who-writes">How each one works</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>The Daily Five</strong> covers five tech stories every morning at 10:00 IST, each one taken apart the same way: The problem, What changed, The catch, What it means for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Known Issue is written by hand.</strong> Swami Guru writes it, and it is reviewed before it is published. It is opinion, and it says so.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Fine Print explainers are tied to a source document.</strong> Each one goes back to the circular, notice or policy behind the change, and carries a "last checked" date.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
      <p>
        Items in the Daily Five link to the pages they rely on: the original article, or a primary document such as a filing, press release or support page. If a real source page was not found for an item, it carries no source link rather than a guessed one. Issues published before October 8, 2026 name their sources in the text without links.
      </p>

      <h2 id="money">Money and independence</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Ads, when they run, are labeled "Advertisement" and sit apart from the writing.</li>
        <li>Anything sponsored is labeled as sponsored. The opinion is not part of any deal.</li>
        <li>Long Press has no embargo access, so nothing is held back for a launch date.</li>
        <li>Long Press does not currently use affiliate links. If that changes, links will be marked on the page and this policy will be updated.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The commercial side is described on the <a href="/about#corrections-and-contact">About page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Mistakes are fixed on the page, with a line saying what changed and when. To report one, write to <a href="mailto:builtbyswami@gmail.com">builtbyswami@gmail.com</a> with the page link and what is wrong. Details are on the <a href="/about#corrections-and-contact">About page</a> and the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
